# campania_transplant — core rules

Dual canonical: keep in sync with [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md).

Inherits global rules from `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` and `~/.cursor/rules/`.

## Disk-efficient dependencies

Use `uv`, the shared cache, and `--link-mode hardlink` with the repo-root `.venv`. Keep cache and repo on the same filesystem; avoid bare `pip`, copy mode, and `--no-cache`.

## Purpose

Budget-impact model and Streamlit dashboard for Campania transplant / PIRP paper. Research / health-economics only — not clinical decision support.

## Stack

- `streamlit`, `matplotlib`, `numpy`, `graphviz`, `python-docx`
- Quick start: `uv venv --python 3.11 .venv`, then `uv pip install --python .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe --link-mode hardlink -r requirements.txt`, then `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m streamlit run app.py`
- **Word COM preferred** for review-grade DOCX writes on Windows; `python-docx` for diff/extract/repair today

## Layout

- `app.py` — Streamlit entrypoint
- `model/` — `params.py`, `engine.py` (equations = source of truth)
- `figures/` — matplotlib builders
- `scripts/` — DOCX tooling (`extract_docx.py`, `compare_docx_versions.py`, etc.)
- `documents/` — read-only source paper inputs

## Repo rules

- Model equations in `model/engine.py` align with paper (Appendix X / Table 17.1).
- Figures regenerate from sliders — no hand-tweaked embeds.
- `requirements.txt` + `packages.txt` lockstep for Streamlit Cloud.

## Repeatable workflows

Document in [`skills.md`](../../skills.md); mirror to `.cursor/skills/` when workflows exist.
